  "analysis": "Both responses address the core requirements—real‑time cache invalidation without global logout, high‑privilege fresh lookups, concurrency safety, and the need for a manual verification script. KPS is more explicit about the CI cost limits (max two full runs), guarantees no public API change, includes a canary rollout and a dedicated performance load test, and tightly ties gates to budget and risk constraints. SXP is also solid but is less detailed on CI budgeting and performance validation, making KPS the more immediately actionable plan.",
